    "q-216328": {
      "dom_id": "step-q216328",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$\\,$ If $P$ and $Q$ are congruent triangles, then $P$ and $Q$ have the same area.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the implication above?\n\n- $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles is a **necessary** condition for $P$ and $Q$ having the same area\n- $P$ and $Q$ having the same area is a **necessary** condition for $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles\n- $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles is a **sufficient** condition for $P$ and $Q$ having the same area\n- $P$ and $Q$ having the same area is a **sufficient** condition for $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles",
      "worked_solution": "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n{{(\\,P\\text{ and }Q\\text{ are congruent triangles}\\,)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,{{(\\,P\\text{ and }Q\\text{ have the same area}\\,)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement II is true. $P$ and $Q$ having the same area is a **necessary** condition for $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles.\n\n- Statement III is true. $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles is a **sufficient** condition for $P$ and $Q$ having the same area.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
