    "q-183396": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183396",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$\\,$ If $A⊂B,$ then $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the implication above?\n\n- $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $A⊂B$\n- $A⊂B$ is a **necessary** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$\n- $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A⊂B$\n- $A⊂B$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$",
      "worked_solution": "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n{{(\\,A⊂B\\,)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,{{(\\,A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅\\,)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement I is true. $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $A⊂B.$\n\n- Statement IV is true. $A⊂B$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"",
